caml_MD5Update takes an uintnat length.

src/stubs-md5.c declares the runtime's caml_MD5Update with an `unsigned`
length where the runtime has `uintnat`: the same type on wasm32, not on
wasm64, where wasm-ld turns the call into a trap (MD5 hashing then stops
with "unreachable").

--- a/src/stubs-md5.c
+++ b/src/stubs-md5.c
@@
 CAMLextern void caml_MD5Update (struct MD5Context *context,
-                           unsigned char *buf, unsigned len);
+                           unsigned char *buf, uintnat len);
